---

import BaseLayout from "../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../styles/projects.css";

---

<BaseLayout title="RFM Customer Segmentation">
  <main class="case-study">

    <p>
      <a href=".."><- Back</a>
    </p>

  <h1>RFM Customer Segmentation</h1>
    <section>
    <h2>Video Demo</h2>

    <a href="https://github.com/KGCraig/RFM-Analysis" target="_blank">
    Download the project on GitHub ->
    </a>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Problem</h2>
    <p>
      Businesses often struggle to understand which customers are most valuable and which are at risk of leaving.
      The goal of this project was to segment customers based on purchasing behavior using RFM analysis.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Data</h2>
    <p>
      The dataset contains transaction history including purchase dates, frequency, and monetary value.
      It was cleaned and aggregated to build customer-level metrics.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Approach</h2>
    <p>
      I used the RFM framework:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Recency:</strong> how recently a customer purchased</li>
      <li><strong>Frequency:</strong> how often they purchase</li>
      <li><strong>Monetary:</strong> how much they spend</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Implementation</h2>
    <p>
      I calculated RFM scores using Python and Pandas, then segmented customers into groups such as
      Champions, Loyal Customers, At Risk, and Lost Customers.
    </p>

    <p>
      Visualization was done using Matplotlib / Plotly to analyze distribution across segments.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Results</h2>
    <p>
      The segmentation revealed clear behavioral clusters:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Champions: high-value frequent buyers</li>
      <li>Loyal Customers: consistent spenders</li>
      <li>At Risk: declining engagement</li>
      <li>Lost Customers: inactive users</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What I Learned</h2>
    <p>
      This project strengthened my understanding of data aggregation, feature engineering,
      and how simple behavioral models can produce actionable business insights.
    </p>
  </section>

  <a href="https://github.com/KGCraig/RFM-Analysis" target="_blank">
    View on GitHub ->
  </a>

</main>
</BaseLayout>